        "subject": "LU-20497 efalnd: Add response cookie to TX to detect stale responses",
        "message": "LU-20497 efalnd: Add response cookie to TX to detect stale responses\n\nWhen a TX is aborted by the daemon and returned to the pool, its slot\ncan be reused for a new request. If a stale GETR_ACK or completion from\nthe original request arrives after we completed the Tx, we fetch a Tx\nusing the index stored in the cookie not used for the message anymore.\nThis can lead to undefined behaviors since the Tx can be freed but also\ncan already be used for another message.\n\nFix by replacing the boolean waiting_resp with an atomic resp_cookie\nthat combines a 31-bit resp_id (incremented per request) and a 1-bit\nvalidity flag. The wire cookie sent to the remote peer embeds the full\nresp_cookie value. On response arrival, it atomically validates the\nresp_cookie matches AND clears validity in a single cmpxchg -\neliminating any race window between validation and claim.\n\nThis makes the stale response detection atomic: if the TX was aborted\n(cmpxchg in abort clears valid first) or recycled (resp_id changed),\nthe response handler's cmpxchg fails and the response is dropped.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Yonatan Nachum <ynachum@amazon.com>\nChange-Id: I78b702995ddfea1c9ce8159b2cbb65255e3a1188\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
